    "title": "How many students were enrolled in Montgomery County schools during 2023-24 school year?",
    "text": "Texas Education Commissioner Mike Morath (2024) | Ballotpedia\nTexas Education Commissioner Mike Morath (2024) | Ballotpedia\nTexas Education Agency.\nAt the time, Montgomery County had the 11th largest enrollment in the state.\nData also showed that white students made up 42.1% of the student body, the largest percentage in Montgomery County schools, followed by Hispanic students at 42.1%, Black students at 8%, Asian students at 3.6%, American Indian students at 0.3%, Pacific Islander students at 0.2% and multiracial students at 3.7%.\nUnderfunding is a frequently cited challenge facing the state's school district. According to a 2024 report from the Texas Education Agency, per-pupil funding has not increased since 2019, despite inflation rates rising by more than 20% since then.\n“As a result, many districts in our very own Central Texas region are being forced to cut back on essential programs, services, consider school closures, and adopt deficit budgets just to provide students with the education that they deserve,” Hutto ISD Trustee James Matlock stated in an interview.\nSchool name | Total enrollment in 2022-23 | Total enrollment in 2023-24 | % change |\n---|---|---|---|\nAnderson Elementary School | 744 | 723 | -2.8% |\nArmstrong Elementary School | 609 | 633 | 3.9% |\nAustin Elementary School | 950 | 1,031 | 8.5% |\nBear Branch Elementary School | 579 | 568 | -1.9% |\nBear Branch Intermediate School | 1,017 | 1,019 | 0.2% |\nBear Branch Junior High School | 1,076 | 1,077 | 0.1% |\nBens Branch Elementary School | 725 | 775 | 6.9% |\nBirnham Woods Elementary School | 996 | 899 | -9.7% |\nBooker T. Washington High School | 166 | 173 | 4.2% |\nBozman Intermediate School | 988 | 1,001 | 1.3% |\nBradley Elementary School | 1,041 | 1,022 | -1.8% |\nBroadway Elementary School | 1,351 | 998 | -26.1% |\nBrookwood Forest Elementary School | 942 | 796 | -15.5% |\nBuckalew Elementary School | 702 | 743 | 5.8% |\nBush Elementary School | 880 | 895 | 1.7% |\n